version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
keywords:
  - heavy rare earth elements
  - yttrium
  - stream sediment geochemistry
  - Mesoproterozoic
  - ferroan granite
  - permutation testing
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline for a study testing whether the lithologic period of
  intrusive igneous terrain predicts acid-leachable yttrium concentration in
  the stream sediment draining it, using 32,221 reanalyzed NURE-HSSR samples
  across six western United States states. Significance is assessed by a
  blocked permutation test that permutes the period label by 150 kilometer
  spatial blocks within state, preserving both the spatial structure and the
  provincial composition of the sample.
